 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nOAuth1 authorization endpoint returns wrong status codes and response format\n\n#### Description\n\nThe OAuth1 authorization endpoint is returning incorrect HTTP status codes and response formats. When creating authorization responses, the endpoint returns 201 instead of 200 for out-of-band (oob) callbacks and 301 instead of 302 for regular redirects.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom oauthlib.oauth1 import AuthorizationEndpoint\nfrom oauthlib.oauth1.rfc5849 import RequestValidator\n\nclass MockValidator(RequestValidator):\n    def verify_request_token(self, token, request):\n        return True\n    \n    def get_redirect_uri(self, token, request):\n        return 'oob'  # or return 'https://example.com/callback'\n\nvalidator = MockValidator()\nendpoint = AuthorizationEndpoint(validator)\n\n# For oob callback - should return 200 but returns 201\nuri = 'https://example.com/authorize?oauth_token=test_token'\nheaders, body, status = endpoint.create_authorization_response(uri)\nprint(f\"OOB Status: {status}\")  # Expected: 200, Actual: 201\n\n# For regular redirect - should return 302 but returns 301  \nvalidator.get_redirect_uri = lambda token, request: 'https://example.com/callback'\nheaders, body, status = endpoint.create_authorization_response(uri)\nprint(f\"Redirect Status: {status}\")  # Expected: 302, Actual: 301\n```\n\nThe authorization endpoint also has issues with token verification logic and response body formatting that affect the OAuth1 flow.\n</issue>\n",
